# Caddy reverse proxy for the runtime control plane on instance A.
#
# Public HTTPS entrypoint for runtime.sausheong.com. Caddy obtains and renews a
# Let's Encrypt certificate automatically over HTTP-01/TLS-ALPN — this requires:
#   - the domain's A record points at instance A's static public IP, and
#   - ports 80 and 443 are reachable from the internet (firewall
#     runtime-allow-https, scoped to the runtime-https network tag).
#
# Everything proxies to runtimed:8080 — both the console (/ui) and the
# control-plane API (/) live on that single port. No Google load balancer and no
# Google-managed certificate: TLS terminates in this Caddy container, so the
# setup stays cloud-agnostic (same config runs on any Docker host).
#
# SECURITY: this exposes the control plane to the public internet. It is safe
# ONLY because runtime identity is ON (RUNTIME_ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP set on runtimed):
# every /ui and API request is authenticated. The dashboards (Grafana :3000,
# Jaeger :16686, Prometheus :9090) and runtimed :8080 are NOT proxied here and
# remain reachable only over the IAP tunnel.
{
	email {$ACME_EMAIL:admin@sausheong.com}
}

{$SITE_ADDRESS:runtime.sausheong.com} {
	encode gzip
	reverse_proxy runtimed:8080
}
